      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sodus Point sits on a peninsula at the northwest edge of Sodus Bay, the southern shore of Lake Ontario.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodus_Point%2C_New_York",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village was first settled in 1794, making it the earliest European‑American community in the Town of Sodus.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodus_Point%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the War of 1812, a British raiding party burned the village, an event that still echoes in local lore.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodus_Point%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 19th century, Sodus Point grew into a bustling Lake Ontario port, later becoming a popular summer resort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodus_Point%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The historic Customs House, built by Sylvanus Macy as a private bank, later housed a U.S. Customs Office and post office.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodus_Point%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The schooner Lotus, the Customs House, and the Sodus Point Light are all listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
